<p>This function allows you to convert the colors used in a document to 
 the barrier-free colors applicable to Color Universal Design (CUD).</p>
<p>You can print the document in the converted colors so that people with 
 various types of color vision can distinguish the colors easily.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only for color printers.</p></li>
<li><p>The color tone of the print result might differ 
 considerably from the color tone of the original.</p></li>
<li><p>If you select this function, <span class="Term-Soft">Barrier-free 
 Color Management</span> is automatically selected for <span class="Term-Soft">Color Profile:</span> on the <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Image Quality/Color</span> 
 tab.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Barrier-free Color 
 Management:</span> list, select <span class="Term-Soft">On</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
